Reference renderer: 8 bit render targets (LIN_L8) are one byte a pixel; headless draws them every frame

The title's dynamic gamma draws its 40x60 luminance measurement into a LIN_L8 target and reads it on the CPU. The
plane code wrote 16 bit RGB565 values there (two bytes over each one byte pixel), so on drawn frames the histogram read
noise; and the headless backend rasterises only snapshot frames (clears run always), so on the others the title read
a cleared target. Its gamma ramp sank to black (FINDINGS.md "Dynamic gamma"). An 8 bit plane now stores the blue
channel (the console's B8 surface), and draws into 8 bit linear targets run on every headless frame.

